      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Squeezed light turns quantum noise into a practical resource for precision interferometry. Its use in gravitational-wave detection has enabled measurements that would otherwise be less sensitive.",
        "attribution": "Caves supplied foundational theory, Kimble helped establish experimental quantum optics methods, and Mavalvala led key interferometric demonstrations. Several contributors on the list represent distinct strands of this achievement.",
        "maturity": "The technique is operating in gravitational-wave observatories, with measurable sensitivity gains and ongoing improvements.",
        "uncertainties": [
