      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Atom interferometry extended matter-wave interference into a highly sensitive measurement method for acceleration, rotation, and fundamental constants.",
        "attribution": "The named researchers represent important early development and experimental realization, but the field grew through many groups and related techniques.",
        "maturity": "Laboratory demonstrations are strong, and instruments are advancing toward field use. Some applications remain less mature than optical frequency metrology.",
